# lws_context_init_ssl_library allocates a pthread_mutex table for OpenSSL's
# pre-1.1 locking callbacks (lib/tls/openssl/openssl-tls.c, the LWS_MAX_SMP != 1
# block) once per process and never frees it: OpenSSL 1.1+ ignores the callbacks
# and lws has no teardown for the table. Process-lifetime by design, not growth.
leak:lws_context_init_ssl_library
